# Code owners for review routing. The owner publishes under the organisation
# only, so no personal handle appears here. GitHub resolves a team owner only
# when the team exists and has write access: create the team "maintainers" in
# the OpenVAPT organisation (Settings > Teams > New team, add the owner, give
# it Write on this repository), then the ruleset may require a code owner
# review for the paths below (docs/adr/0010-branch-ruleset.md).
# Until the team exists these lines resolve to nobody and do not block.

# Release pipeline, channel gates and the evidence they trust
/.github/                 @OpenVAPT/maintainers
/cmd/channel/             @OpenVAPT/maintainers
/internal/channels/       @OpenVAPT/maintainers
/release/                 @OpenVAPT/maintainers
/scripts/install.sh       @OpenVAPT/maintainers
/Makefile                 @OpenVAPT/maintainers

# Safety boundaries (AGENTS.md section 4)
/internal/scope/          @OpenVAPT/maintainers
/internal/sys/            @OpenVAPT/maintainers
/internal/redact/         @OpenVAPT/maintainers

# Legal texts (AGENTS.md section 3.6)
/LICENSE                  @OpenVAPT/maintainers
/EULA.md                  @OpenVAPT/maintainers
/ACCEPTABLE_USE.md        @OpenVAPT/maintainers
/DISCLAIMER.md            @OpenVAPT/maintainers
/PRIVACY.md               @OpenVAPT/maintainers
/LICENSING.md             @OpenVAPT/maintainers
/NOTICE                   @OpenVAPT/maintainers
/internal/terms/          @OpenVAPT/maintainers
